Hi Edwin,

Thanks for your question.

If you're seeing that WARN message, you're in the default hybrid_warn mode
and shouldn't experience any change in operating behavior. That message may
be unrelated/a distraction from the problem you're experiencing.

> I have explicitly defined the plugin.path in my
connect-distributed.properties as such:
> plugin.path=3D~/kafka_2.13-4.0.0/plugins ,where my
mariadb-java-client-3.5.5 jar is present.

Can you be more explicit about your directory structure, and/or can you
post more of the WARN message?
You may also consider enabling debug or trace logging for
the org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.isolation package.

Also, do you have a similar plugin.path set for v3.7.1 as you do for
v4.0.0? Or is the plugin.path something you changed to try and mitigate the
WARN message?

Thanks,
Greg

