Hi Ismael,

If I understand your question, in KIP-392 the `client.rack` config serve=
s both as setting the rack and as the on/off switch for the whole featur=
e. In KIP-1123, these are separate. Originally I thought that having sep=
arate configs would be more explicit and more future-proof: in case some=
 other new feature that rely on the `client.rack` setting is added. Do y=
ou think I should change it to the single config to be uniform with KIP-=
392?

Best,
Ivan


On Sun, Jul 20, 2025, at 23:15, Ismael Juma wrote:
> Hi,
>=20
> Thanks for the KIP. One question I have is why two configs are needed
> instead of a single config? KIP-392 specifies a single client side con=
fig.
> It would be good to be consistent across the clients.
>=20
> Ismael
>=20
> On Fri, Dec 20, 2024 at 3:37=E2=80=AFAM Ivan Yurchenko <ivan@ivanyu.me=
> wrote:
