Miko=C5=82aj Bul created KAFKA-19724:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: Global stream thread ignores all exceptions
                 Key: KAFKA-19724
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19724
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: streams
    Affects Versions: 3.4.0
            Reporter: Miko=C5=82aj Bul


{{globalStreamThread}} in {{KafkaStreams}} class ignores all exceptions and=
 fails to apply the user-provided {{StreamsUncaughtExceptionHandler}} in:
{code:java}
public void setUncaughtExceptionHandler(final StreamsUncaughtExceptionHandl=
er userStreamsUncaughtExceptionHandler)
{code}
This can lead to streams being stuck in faulty state after an exception is =
thrown during their initialization phase (e.g. failure to load the RocksDB =
native library).

>From my understanding of the=C2=A0{{b62d8b97}} commit message, the followin=
g code is unnecessary as the {{globalStreamThread}} can't be replaced and i=
ssue description from KAFKA-12699 doesn't apply to it. Removing it should h=
elp.
{code:java}
if (globalStreamThread !=3D null) {
    globalStreamThread.setUncaughtExceptionHandler((t, e) -> { }
    );
}
{code}



