--0000000000006523c8063f292c9c
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Our team is looking to move to the latest 3.x version of Kafka. The latest
available, version 3.9.1, currently has the high score  CVE-2025-48734. The
culprit is a dependency on commons-beanutils-1.9.4.jar.

Are there any future plans to mitigate this CVE in a 3.9.x update?

